  "rationale": "The batch contains a recurring opening idiom, “Long ago,” but the target ago has extremely low probability; the existing generic ago rule contributes little in that context. Add a reusable Long-to-ago continuation and raise comma after ago, both supported by the observed sequence. The concluding phrase “was the end” also has a very low-probability end target, so add a context-specific noun continuation. Long following a noun and paragraph space generalizes the observed temporal-opening pattern without depending on the particular noun. These rules are limited to observed grammatical contexts; other continuations remain possible, and the batch is too small to establish that every Long or every paragraph break requires these words. Replay behavior has not been verified."
